---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL } from '../../data/site-config';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title="Privacy Policy of NZSalary.com: What We Collect and Why" description="Privacy policy of NZSalary.com: calculations run in your browser, no cookies, no visitor records, hosting logs and a cookieless Clarity stability check." lang={lang} noindex={true} jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'Privacy', path: route('privacy', lang) }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Privacy' }]}>
  <header class="mb-6"><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-900 md:text-4xl">Privacy policy</h1></header>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang="en" />
    <h2>What happens to the numbers you type</h2>
    <p>Nothing leaves your device. Gross pay, tax code, KiwiSaver rate, student loan: the PAYE engine works them through in your browser, so they never reach us or anyone else, are saved on no server and cannot be connected to you. No account, newsletter or form exists to gather personal information. Once you edit a field, the address bar carries your values so the link can be shared; only the people who receive that link see them.</p>
    <h2>What the host sees</h2>
    <p>{LEGAL.hosting.name} serves the pages. Each request leaves a standard log entry (IP address, page, time, browser type) that the host keeps to run and protect the service. We make no use of those entries to identify anyone.</p>
    <h2>No cookies, no visitor records</h2>
    <p>NZSalary.com sets no cookie and stores nothing on your device. The publisher keeps no personal information about the people who visit and runs no audience analytics.</p>
    <h2>Stability check: Microsoft Clarity without cookies</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What it sees:</strong> script errors, load times, dead clicks, scroll depth, device and browser type. Page text and form entries are masked before leaving the browser; the page address it notes can still contain the values of a shared calculator link.</li>
      <li><strong>How it runs:</strong> storage is refused before the script loads, so no cookie is written (no <code>_clck</code>, <code>_clsk</code>, <code>MUID</code> or <code>CLID</code>), each page view has its own identifier and visits are not linked.</li>
      <li><strong>Who runs it:</strong> Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland. Recordings are kept 30 days and aggregates 13 months, possibly outside New Zealand, for instance in the United States (see the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a>).</li>
      <li><strong>Why:</strong> a legitimate interest in keeping the calculators working (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR, the publisher being in France), a purpose connected with running the site as the Privacy Act 2020 expects.</li>
      <li><strong>Opting out:</strong> block clarity.ms, or write to us; the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a> has the detail. The calculators behave the same without it.</li>
      <li>No advertising script runs on NZSalary.com.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>The Privacy Act 2020 lets you ask any agency for access to, and correction of, personal information it holds about you; because the publisher is in France, the GDPR applies as well. We hold none from the calculators, but you can still write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. If the answer does not satisfy you, contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner or France’s {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
